adaptation-samsung-r7 (0.0.0+git20260720203123.c4c06d0.bookworm+git20260728092037.c349ebc.bookworm+r7spen1+r7dns1+r7setup2+r7ssh1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Ship a working SSH server out of the box. The base image installs NO SSH
    server (only client libs), so a fresh flash had the "Secure Shell" toggle
    but nothing behind it (ssh.service did not exist -> the toggle reverted) and
    NO remote access at all, which matters because USB RNDIS is unreliable on
    this device. The metapackage now Depends on openssh-server.
  * Add r7-regenerate-ssh-host-keys.service (first-boot oneshot, ordered before
    sshd binds, stamped): installing openssh-server at image-build time bakes
    host keys into the public image, so every device would share them; this
    wipes and regenerates per-device keys on first boot instead.

